1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,913
Now the twist.

2
00:00:01,933 --> 00:00:03,033
The second is over,

3
00:00:03,053 --> 00:00:04,184
and Earth starts spinning

4
00:00:04,184 --> 00:00:05,211
again, instantly.

5
00:00:05,231 --> 00:00:06,707
Anything still flying east is

6
00:00:06,707 --> 00:00:08,012
suddenly back in sync with

7
00:00:08,012 --> 00:00:08,789
the ground.

8
00:00:08,809 --> 00:00:09,838
Lucky.

9
00:00:09,858 --> 00:00:10,929
But everything that crashed

10
00:00:10,929 --> 00:00:12,557
and stopped during that second?

11
00:00:12,577 --> 00:00:13,956
The ground races back under

12
00:00:13,956 --> 00:00:15,067
it at full speed.

13
00:00:15,087 --> 00:00:17,139
So the whole disaster happens again...

14
00:00:17,159 --> 00:00:18,391
in the other direction.

15
00:00:19,741 --> 00:00:21,188
Physics would like a word.

16
00:00:21,208 --> 00:00:22,788
Earth's spin stores about

17
00:00:22,788 --> 00:00:26,218
2×10²⁹ joules of energy.

18
00:00:26,238 --> 00:00:27,569
Stopping it means dumping all

19
00:00:27,569 --> 00:00:28,504
of that somewhere.

20
00:00:28,524 --> 00:00:29,574
That's roughly what the Sun

21
00:00:29,574 --> 00:00:31,029
pours out in nine minutes.

22
00:00:31,049 --> 00:00:31,937
All of the Sun.

23
00:00:33,287 --> 00:00:35,348
And if Earth never started again?

24
00:00:35,368 --> 00:00:36,371
One day would last a

25
00:00:36,371 --> 00:00:37,065
whole year.

26
00:00:37,085 --> 00:00:38,565
Six months of daylight,

27
00:00:38,585 --> 00:00:39,959
then six months of night.

28
00:00:39,979 --> 00:00:40,925
And the Sun would rise

29
00:00:40,925 --> 00:00:41,720
in the west.

30
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:42,600
Over time,

31
00:00:42,620 --> 00:00:43,599
the oceans would migrate

32
00:00:43,599 --> 00:00:44,680
toward the poles,

33
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:46,025
leaving one giant continent

34
00:00:46,025 --> 00:00:48,073
wrapped around the equator.
